1. Unit test (credit accumulation attack): Create a budget with max_inflation_ratio = 10. Feed two entries: first entry has 1000 compressed bytes and 1000 decompressed bytes (ratio 1:1, stored). Second entry has 1 compressed byte. Without per-entry ratio, the second entry can decompress up to 1001 * 10 = 10010 bytes. With per-entry ratio, it can only decompress 1 * 10 = 10 bytes. Verify the second entry hits InflationRatioExceeded.

2. Unit test (first-read probe): When entry_compressed_in = 0 (no compressed data yet), the implementation uses 1 as the denominator. Verify the first read is capped to max_ratio bytes.

3. Integration test: Build a tar containing a stored entry (1:1) followed by a gzip-bomb entry. Verify the bomb entry is stopped by per-entry ratio, not per-archive ratio.

## Property Test Invariants

```rust
proptest! {
    #[test]
    fn entry_ratio_bounded(
        comp_in in 1u64..=10_000,
        reads in prop::collection::vec(1u64..=10_000, 1..=50),
        max_ratio in 2u32..=256,
    ) {
        let cfg = ArchiveConfig {
            max_inflation_ratio: max_ratio,
            max_uncompressed_bytes_per_entry: u64::MAX - 1,
            ..ArchiveConfig::default()
        };
        let mut b = ArchiveBudgets::new(&cfg);
        b.enter_archive().unwrap();
        b.begin_entry_scan();
        b.charge_compressed_in(comp_in);
        let mut total_out = 0u64;
        for &n in &reads {
            match b.charge_decompressed_out(n) {
                ChargeResult::Ok => total_out += n,
                ChargeResult::Clamp { allowed, .. } => { total_out += allowed; break; }
            }
        }
        prop_assert!(total_out <= comp_in.saturating_mul(max_ratio as u64));
    }
}
```

