```

Trait change:
```rust
pub trait ArchiveEntrySink {
    type Error;
    fn on_entry_start(&mut self, meta: &EntryMeta<'_>) -> Result<(), Self::Error>;
    fn on_entry_chunk(&mut self, chunk: EntryChunk<'_>) -> Result<(), Self::Error>;
    fn on_entry_end(&mut self, summary: EntryEndSummary) -> Result<(), Self::Error>;
}
```

Breaking API change. All three sink implementations must be updated:

| Implementation | File | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| UringArchiveSink | src/scheduler/local_fs_uring.rs ~line 727 | Can log summary for observability |
| SimArchiveSink | src/sim_scanner/runner.rs | Record summary for simulation assertions |
| RecordingSink | src/archive/scan_tests.rs | Store summaries for test verification |

Construction is zero-cost: All three loops already track offset (bytes delivered) and entry_partial_reason. The ratio can be computed from entry_decompressed_out / entry_compressed_in (available after Task 2 adds per-entry tracking). If Task 2 is not yet done, ratio can be left as 0.

Loop changes (one per format — gzip, tar, zip):

Before each sink.on_entry_end() call, construct the summary from loop-local variables:

```rust
