## Problem

Fresh DeflateDecoder per zip entry allocates ~72KB each (40KB zlib-ng state + 32KB BufReader). For archives with many small deflate entries (e.g., 1000 .class files in a JAR), this is ~72MB of allocation churn.

## Research: This Codebase Already Has 3 Working Implementations

The decoder pooling pattern already exists in three places in this codebase:

| Location | Pattern | Reset Call |
|---|---|---|
| src/git_scan/pack_inflate.rs:38-87 | Thread-local RefCell<InflateScratch> with Decompress + 64KB buffer | de.reset(true) at lines 464, 571 |
| src/git_scan/pack_exec.rs:1065-1071 | Per-plan DecodeBufs with de: flate2::Decompress passed as &mut | Reset in inflate_limited_with |
| src/object_store.rs:313-354 | Per-store TreeDecodeBufs with Decompress + detach_recursive_scratch | de.reset(true) internally |

All three use plain fields (not Option), call de.reset(zlib_header) per stream, and operate in single-threaded contexts matching ArchiveScratch's ownership model.

## The flate2 Reset API

```rust
// flate2::Decompress::reset(zlib_header: bool)
